@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s48-area-order`
IMPORT `ito-s48a-foreign-worker-regs`
IMPORT `ito-il28-routing`
IMPORT `ito-il28-test-people`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-28 tests: s 48 and the Area order of 5755-1995 (ss 34, 36, 37 for a resident of the Area
-- who is not an Israeli citizen).
--
-- Every expected value below was worked by hand from the Hebrew text BEFORE the code was run; the arithmetic is
-- in the comment beside it. A failing assertion is a finding: none has been edited to match the code.
-- The sentences relied on:
--   s 34  (ITO line 1570): an individual who was an Israeli resident in the tax year: two credit points.
--   s 36  (line 1594): an individual Israeli resident: a quarter point as a travel credit.
--   s 36A (line 1597): a woman: half a point.   s 37 (line 1600): a favoured individual who proved his spouse's
--   livelihood was upon him: one point.
--   ORD s 1 (line 15): ss 34, 36 and 37 apply also to residents of the Area who are not Israeli citizens, as if
--   they were Israeli residents. s 36A is not named.
-- Lettering of readings: A first listed, B second, D declined (ito-il28-test-people.l4).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — s 48 and the Order of 5755-1995`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total` t `under` r MEANS `the total credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s34` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 34 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s36` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 36 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s36A` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 36A in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s37` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 37 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

§§ `Who is reached`

-- s 3A(a): an Israeli citizen is (1) a citizen, (2) an Israeli resident, (3) one entitled to immigrate under the
-- Law of Return who is a resident of the Area. The Order reaches a resident of the Area who is none of these.
#ASSERT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `an Area man`
#ASSERT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `an Area woman`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` `an Area man`
#ASSERT `the taxpayer is an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` `an Israeli citizen resident in the Area`
#ASSERT `the taxpayer is an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` `a resident of the Area entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`
#ASSERT `the taxpayer is an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` `a resident of the Area who is also an Israeli resident`
-- (3) needs both limbs: entitled to immigrate AND a resident of the Area.
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` `a person entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return who is not a resident of the Area`
#ASSERT NOT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `an Israeli citizen resident in the Area`
#ASSERT NOT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `a resident of the Area entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`
#ASSERT NOT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `a resident of the Area who is also an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT NOT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `a person entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return who is not a resident of the Area`
#ASSERT NOT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `a man with no tie to the Area`
-- ss 34, 36 and 37 speak of an individual: a company resident in the Area is not reached.
#ASSERT NOT `the Order reaches the taxpayer` `an Area company`
#ASSERT `the instrument that reaches` `an Area man` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `the Area order reaches the taxpayer`
#ASSERT `the instrument that reaches` `an Area company` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`
#ASSERT `the instrument that reaches` `an Israeli citizen resident in the Area` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`

-- A person the Order does not reach is not answered by this row: the ordinary sections govern.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Israeli citizen resident in the Area` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a man with no tie to the Area` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points the Order gives to` `a man with no tie to the Area` `, under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Order does not reach the taxpayer, so its points are not asked"

§§ `An Area man — ss 34 and 36 by the Order`

-- s 34: 2.  s 36: 1/4 (he has income from personal exertion, so fork F2 does not arise).  s 36A: not a woman, 0.
-- s 37: none of its facts, 0.  Total 2 + 1/4 + 0 + 0 = 9/4.
#ASSERT `s34` `an Area man` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s36` `an Area man` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `s36A` `an Area man` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s37` `an Area man` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 9/4

§§ `An Area woman — s 36A is not named by the Order (fork F1)`

-- The Order names ss 34, 36 and 37, not s 36A, which has no residence limb of its own. Whether she gets its half point
-- is fork F1 (carried from row IL-01): A, no residence condition: 1/2; B, only to an Israeli resident: she is by
-- s 3A(a)(2) never one, so 0; D, declined. Ss 34 and 36 are unaffected: 2 and 1/4.
#ASSERT `s34` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s36` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36A` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point"
-- A: 2 + 1/4 + 1/2 = 11/4.   B: 2 + 1/4 + 0 = 9/4.
#ASSERT `s36A` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings but F1 is A` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `total` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings but F1 is A` EQUALS 11/4
#ASSERT `s36A` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings but F1 is B` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `an Area woman` `under` `the default readings but F1 is B` EQUALS 9/4

§§ `Section 37 under the Order`

-- A favoured individual whose spouse's livelihood was upon him and who proved it: one point.
-- Total 2 + 1/4 + 0 + 1 = 13/4.
#ASSERT `s37` `an Area man with a dependent spouse, a favoured individual, proved` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man with a dependent spouse, a favoured individual, proved` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 13/4
-- Each of the three conditions failing alone: no point. Total 9/4.
#ASSERT `s37` `an Area man whose spouse's dependence is not proved` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s37` `an Area man whose spouse is not dependent` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s37` `an Area man who is not a favoured individual` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man whose spouse's dependence is not proved` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 9/4

§§ `Section 36 and income from personal exertion (fork F2)`

-- D: declined. A: every individual, 1/4, total 9/4. B: only with such income: 0, total 2 + 0 = 2.
#ASSERT `s34` `an Area man without income from personal exertion` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36` `an Area man without income from personal exertion` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area man without income from personal exertion` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point"
#ASSERT `s36` `an Area man without income from personal exertion` `under` `the default readings but F2 is A` EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man without income from personal exertion` `under` `the default readings but F2 is A` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `s36` `an Area man without income from personal exertion` `under` `the default readings but F2 is B` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man without income from personal exertion` `under` `the default readings but F2 is B` EQUALS 2

§§ `A resident of the Area for only part of the tax year (fork F4)`

-- D: ss 34 and 36 differ between the two readings (2 against 2 x 6/12 = 1; 1/4 against 1/4 x 6/12 = 1/8): declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s34` `an Area man resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Order does not say what a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year gets"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36` `an Area man resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Order does not say what a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year gets"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area man resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Order does not say what a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year gets"
-- A: one status for the year, 2 + 1/4 = 9/4.
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings but F4 is A` EQUALS 9/4
-- B, as s 41(1) apportions ss 34 and 36 by months: 6 months: 2 x 6/12 = 1; 1/4 x 6/12 = 1/8; total 9/8.
#ASSERT `s34` `an Area man resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings but F4 is B` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s36` `an Area man resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings but F4 is B` EQUALS 1/8
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings but F4 is B` EQUALS 9/8
-- 11 months: 2 x 11/12 = 11/6; 1/4 x 11/12 = 11/48; total 88/48 + 11/48 = 99/48 = 33/16.
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man resident in the Area for 11 months` `under` `the default readings but F4 is B` EQUALS 33/16
-- 1 month: 2/12 = 1/6 = 8/48; 1/4 x 1/12 = 1/48; total 9/48 = 3/16.
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man resident in the Area for 1 month` `under` `the default readings but F4 is B` EQUALS 3/16
-- s 36A has no residence limb, so it is not apportioned: a woman, 6 months, F4 B and F1 A: 1 + 1/8 + 1/2 = 13/8.
#ASSERT `total` `an Area woman resident in the Area for 6 months` `under` `the default readings but F4 is B and F1 is A` EQUALS 13/8
-- A part-year count outside 1 to 11 is not a part of a year.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s34` `an Area man resident in the Area for 0 months` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the months of residence in the Area must be a whole number from 1 to 11"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s34` `an Area man resident in the Area for 12 months entered as part of a year` `under` `the default readings but F4 is B` BECAUSE "the months of residence in the Area must be a whole number from 1 to 11"

§§ `The tax years`

-- The Order is of 1 March 1995; orders under s 48 before it are not deposited.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area man in 1994` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds no order under section 48 for a tax year before 1995"
-- 1995 to 2016: s 3A, whose three terms s 48 adopts, was last amended in 5776 (Hebrew year ended 2 October 2016): the
-- deposited text governs from the tax year 2017 (the rule row IL-01 uses, its fork F12); and the Order has no commencement clause,
-- so its start within 1995 is not stated.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area man in 1995` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds neither section 3A as it stood before 2017 nor the Order's start within 1995"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area man in 2016` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds neither section 3A as it stood before 2017 nor the Order's start within 1995"
-- 2017 to 2022: ss 34, 36 and 36A answer, s 37 (last amended in 5782, ended 25 September 2022) does not: from 2023 only.
#ASSERT `s34` `an Area man in 2017` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A alone in place of the ordinary sections for` `an Area man in 2017` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT REFUSED `s37` `an Area man in 2017` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds section 37 as it stood only from the tax year 2023"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area man in 2022` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds section 37 as it stood only from the tax year 2023"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Area man with a dependent spouse, a favoured individual, proved, in 2022` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds section 37 as it stood only from the tax year 2023"
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man in 2023` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `total` `an Area man with a dependent spouse, a favoured individual, proved, in 2023` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 13/4

§§ `What the Order does to each provision of Chapter Three`

-- ORD s 1 names ss 34, 36 and 37 and no other section.
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 34` EQUALS `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 36` EQUALS `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 37` EQUALS `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 36A` EQUALS `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 40` EQUALS `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 38` EQUALS `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 46` EQUALS `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`
#ASSERT `what the Order does to` `section 47, a deduction` EQUALS `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`
#ASSERT `what the instrument that reaches` `an Area man` `, under` `the default readings` `, does to` `section 34` EQUALS `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT REFUSED `what the instrument that reaches` `a man with no tie to the Area` `, under` `the default readings` `, does to` `section 34` BECAUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"

§§ `The amount in NIS`

-- Illustrative input only: NIS 2,904 per credit point, the figure row IL-01 carries from the Israel Tax Authority for
-- 2025 (a published figure, not law). 9/4 x 2904 = 6534. 11/4 x 2904 = 7986. 13/4 x 2904 = 9438.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `an Area man` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 EQUALS 6534
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `an Area woman` `, under` `the default readings but F1 is A` `, at` 2904 EQUALS 7986
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `an Area man with a dependent spouse, a favoured individual, proved` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 EQUALS 9438
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `an Area woman` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 BECAUSE "section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point"
